tent="1-143197">Learn more about Telford &amp; Wrekin Climate Action Investment</div><div data-ai-no-open-words="" data-content="1-143198">Telford &amp; Wrekin launched its first investment in 2023, raising £339,000 Sign up for updates to learn more about this way of investing, and to get updates on new municipal investments as they launch.</div><div data-ai-no-open-button-text="" data-content="1-143199">Sign up for updates</div><div data-ai-no-open-button-url="" data-content="1-143200">/signup-for-updates</div><div data-ai-no-past-invest-header="" data-content="1-143201">Placeholder</div><div data-ai-no-past-invest-copy="" data-content="1-143202">placeholder</div><div data-ai-no-past-invest-button-url="" data-content="1-143203">/</div><div data-ai-no-past-invest-button-text="" data-content="1-143204">Learn more</div><div data-ai-no-chart-img-url="" data-content="1-143205">https://cdn4.sharein.com/abundance/cms/fd81e4f6-d21a-4e91-84fd-4b7e41b130f2.jpg</div><div data-ai-no-chart-img-alt="" data-content="1-143206">An image of a greening project</div><div data-ai-no-chart-img-caption="" data-content="2-143207">The council has been investing in greening projects across the borough</div></div><section class="position-relative bg-colour--primary-surface p-t-spacer-4xl type-white ai-hero" style="background:#8c1f3d"><div class="container"><div class="row brand-media-box align-items-start"><div class="col-12 col-md-8"><h1 class="text-choke-md--640 text-center--md font-secondary" style="color:#fff" data-content="1-143208">Telford &amp; Wrekin Council</h1><p class="body--xl text-choke-md--640 text-center--md m-b-spacer-sm" style="color:#fff" data-content="2-143212">Telford &amp; Wrekin Council is supporting residents, businesses, and community groups to create a carbon neutral borough.</p></div><div class="col-12 col-md-4"><div class="ai-heroLogoRail"><img class="image-responsive hero-header__illustration brand-media-box__img" src="https://cdn4.sharein.com/abundance/cms/11467487-30bf-49ce-b8d7-2c2196abc5ac.png" alt="Camden Council logo" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high"></div></div></div></div></section><div class="bg-colour--primary-surface bg-mask bg-mask--b-convex m-b-spacer-2xl ai-hero-mask" style="background:#8c1f3d"></div><div id="ai-scope-wrap"><section class="m-b-spacer-lg ai-scope"><div class="container text-choke-960"><div class="row"><div class="col-12 text-center" data-content="2-143217"><p class="body--xl">Telford &amp; Wrekin Climate Action Investment was created to allow anyone to support Telford &amp; Wrekin Council’s plans to create a carbon neutral borough. The council is already taking action on its own environmental impact – it has cut its carbon footprint by 58% since 2018, putting it on track to hit its target of becoming carbon neutral by 2030.<br><br> But its plans go far beyond that. It wants to ensure it supports everyone across the borough to take climate action, and this investment allowed the public to back a number of important local climate projects.</p></div></div></div></section><div class="bg-colour--primary-surface bg-mask bg-mask--t-convex ai-no-open-mask ai-scope" style="background-color: rgb(255, 237, 204);"></div><section class="home-green-investing position-relative p-y-spacer-xs bg-colour--primary-surface ai-no-open ai-scope" style="background-color: rgb(255, 237, 204);"><div class="container"><div class="row"><div class="col-12"><div class="flex-center"><h2 class="text-center m-b-spacer-sm">Learn more about Telford &amp; Wrekin Climate Action Investment</h2></div><div class="flex-center"><p class="body--lg text-center choke-800 m-b-spacer-sm">Telford &amp; Wrekin launched its first investment in 2023, raising £339,000 Sign up for updates to learn more about this way of investing, and to get updates on new municipal investments as they launch.</p></div><div class="flex-center ai-no-open-btn-wrap"><a href="/signup-for-updates" class="brand-btn-grey--bordered brand-btn-grey--bordered--bordered btn btn--lg m-y-spacer-md btn--icon" style="border-color:#4c4c4a;color:#4c4c4a">Sign up for updates</a></div></div></div></div></section><div class="bg-colour--primary-surface bg-mask bg-mask--b-convex ai-no-open-mask ai-scope" style="background-color: rgb(255, 237, 204);"></div><div class="bg-colour--primary-surface bg-mask bg-mask--t-convex ai-open-bg ai-scope" style="display: none;"></div><section class="home-green-investing position-relative p-y-spacer-xs ai-open-bg ai-scope" style="display: none;"><div class="container"><div class="row"><div class="col-12"><div class="flex-center"><h2 class="text-center m-b-spacer-sm" data-content="1-143209">Invest in [investment name] today</h2></div><div class="flex-center"><div class="ai-custom ai-open-investments"><div id="ai-open-councils"></div></div></div></div></div></div></section><div class="bg-colour--primary-surface bg-mask bg-mask--b-convex ai-open-bg ai-scope" style="display: none;"></div><section class="home-financial m-y-spacer-md p-y-spacer-xl mx-auto choke-800 ai-scope"><div class="container"><div class="row"><div class="col-12"><div class="flex-center"><h2 class="text-center" data-content="1-143210">How investors' money has been used</h2></div><div class="flex-center"><p class="body--lg text-center choke-800 m-b-spacer-lg"><span data-content="2-143219">Funds raised from the Telford &amp; Wrekin Climate Investment has been used to fund two main projects. In March 2023, the council purchased two electric vehicle minibuses for our Outdoor Education team to use. The team works with schools from across the borough, taking classes out of their regular education settings to green spaces across Telford and Wrekin and also to our outwards bounds centre – Arthog – on the Welsh Coast.<br><br>The money raised also funded a second round of Telford &amp; Wrekin Council’s Climate Change Fund – which was launched in June 2022. Through the fund, the council wanted to encourage organisations in the borough to take action to reduce their carbon footprint and support a ‘green recovery’ at a local level.</span></p></div><div class="flex-center ai-uof-wrap"><div id="ai-use-of-funds"><div id="council-bar-chart"><div class="cbc-card"><section class="cbc-summary" id="cbc-summary" aria-live="polite"><div class="cbc-summary-inner"><div class="cbc-summary-logo"><a class="cbc-summary-logo-link" href="https://www.abundanceinvestment.com/council/telford-and-wrekin" target="_blank" rel="noopener"><div class="cbc-logo-badge" style="background:#8c1f3d;"><img src="https://cdn4.sharein.com/abundance/cms/9dbb979d-ab5d-448b-976f-29f8b64cf221.png" alt="Telford &amp; Wrekin Council logo"></div></a></div><div class="cbc-summary-lines" role="list"><div class="cbc-summary-line" role="listitem">1 investment</div><div class="cbc-summary-line" role="listitem">£339k spent</div><div class="cbc-summary-line" role="listitem">3 projects financed</div></div></div></section><div class="cbc-chart" id="cbc-chart"><div class="cbc-row"><div class="cbc-label">Energy efficiency</div><div class="cbc-bar-wrapper"><div class="cbc-bar-fill" data-final-width="61.6519174041298" style="width: 61.6519%; background: rgb(55, 235, 255);"><span class="cbc-bar-value">61.7%</span></div></div></div><div class="cbc-row"><div class="cbc-label">Clean transportation</div><div class="cbc-bar-wrapper"><div class="cbc-bar-fill" data-final-width="38.34808259587021" style="width: 38.3481%; background: rgb(241, 202, 141);"><span class="cbc-bar-value">38.3%</span></div></div></div></div><section class="cbc-projects"><h3 class="cbc-projects__title">Top projects financed</h3><div class="cbc-projects__list"><details class="cbc-proj"><summary class="cbc-proj__sum"><div class="cbc-proj__pill" style="background:#37ebff;color:#111827;border:1px solid rgba(17,24,39,.10);">Energy Efficiency</div><div class="cbc-proj__titleRow"><h4 class="cbc-proj__name">Climate change fund</h4><div class="cbc-proj__right"><span class="cbc-proj__spent">£200,000.00</span><svg class="cbc-proj__chev" viewBox="0 0 20 20" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path fill="currentColor" d="M5.3 7.3a1 1 0 0 1 1.4 0L10 10.6l3.3-3.3a1 1 0 1 1 1.4 1.4l-4 4a1 1 0 0 1-1.4 0l-4-4a1 1 0 0 1 0-1.4z"></path></svg></div></div></summary><div class="cbc-proj__body"><p>Offers grants to local community projects which seek to operate more sustainably. Through the fund, the council wanted to encourage organisations in the borough to take action to reduce their carbon footprint and support a ‘green recovery’ at a local level beyond the council’s own operations.</p><p>28 successful applicants were awarded funding, totalling more than £217,000. Applicants were also required to find levels of ‘match funding’. This amounted to a further £112.6k, meaning that the project has &nbsp;enabled a total of more than £330,000 to be spent on carbon reductions in the borough. Projects included a wide range of green projects, mostly energy efficiency upgrades. Some of the projects funded are as follows: Sustainable Sunday events at Belmont Hall, Climate Action Hub Telford; solar panels on Hollinswood &amp; Randlay Parish Council; energy efficiency upgrades at Sutton Hill Church; energy efficiency upgrades at Southall School; energy efficiency upgrades at Dawley Town Hall CIC; 2 EV chargers at Fabweld Steel Products Ltd; and recycling improvements at Wrockwardine Wood CE Junior School.</p></div></details><details class="cbc-proj"><summary class="cbc-proj__sum"><div class="cbc-proj__pill" style="background:#f1ca8d;color:#111827;border:1px solid rgba(17,24,39,.10);">Clean Transportation</div><div class="cbc-proj__titleRow"><h4 class="cbc-proj__name">Electrification of community minibus fleet</h4><div class="cbc-proj__right"><span class="cbc-proj__spent">£130,000.00</span><svg class="cbc-proj__chev" viewBox="0 0 20 20" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path fill="currentColor" d="M5.3 7.3a1 1 0 0 1 1.4 0L10 10.6l3.3-3.3a1 1 0 1 1 1.4 1.4l-4 4a1 1 0 0 1-1.4 0l-4-4a1 1 0 0 1 0-1.4z"></path></svg></div></div></summary><div class="cbc-proj__body"><p>Purchase of two electric vehicle minibuses (replacing existing fossil fuel-powered vehicles) for our Outdoor Education team. This team works with schools across the borough to take student out of their regular education settings to green spaces across Telford and Wrekin and also to the Council's outwards bounds centre – Arthog – on the Welsh Coast.</p><p>In these outdoor spaces, children get to experience the natural world and learn about biodiversity and sustainability while also taking part in activities that boost their physical and mental wellbeing.</p></div></details><details class="cbc-proj"><summary class="cbc-proj__sum"><div class="cbc-proj__pill" style="background:#37ebff;color:#111827;border:1px solid rgba(17,24,39,.10);">Energy Efficiency</div><div class="cbc-proj__titleRow"><h4 class="cbc-proj__name">Affordable warmth</h4><div class="cbc-proj__right"><span class="cbc-proj__spent">£9,000.00</span><svg class="cbc-proj__chev" viewBox="0 0 20 20" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path fill="currentColor" d="M5.3 7.3a1 1 0 0 1 1.4 0L10 10.6l3.3-3.3a1 1 0 1 1 1.4 1.4l-4 4a1 1 0 0 1-1.4 0l-4-4a1 1 0 0 1 0-1.4z"></path></svg></div></div></summary><div class="cbc-proj__body"><p>Energy efficiency upgrades to the Council's temporary and supported housing accommodation to deliver a direct carbon saving and ease the financial pressure on these residents, providing them with affordable warmth.</p><p>This project set out to improve the Energy Performance Certificate (EPC) rating of temporary accommodation, which included cavity wall insulation and loft insulation; installation of thermostatic valves was also undertaken.</p></div></details></div></section></div></div></div></div></div></div></div></section><div class="bg-colour--primary-surface bg-mask bg-mask--t-convex ai-scope"></div><section class="home-green-investing position-relative p-y-spacer-xs bg-colour--primary-surface ai-past-wrap ai-scope"><div class="container"><div class="row"><div class="col-12"><div id="ai-past-investments"><div class="flex-center"><h2 class="text-center m-b-spacer-sm">Investment history</h2></div><div class="flex-center"><div class="ai-past-table-choke"><table class="brand-table"><caption>Investment history</caption><thead><tr><th class="brand-table__head" scope="col"><strong>Investment</strong></th><th class="brand-table__head" scope="col"><strong>Interest</strong></th><th class="brand-table__head" scope="col"><strong>Term</strong></th><th class="brand-table__head" scope="col"><strong>Amount raised</strong></th><th class="brand-table__head" scope="col"><strong>Close date</strong></th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td headers="investment" data-title="Investment"><a href="https://www.abundanceinvestment.com/invest/telford-wrekin-climate-action-investment-2027" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Telford &amp; Wrekin Climate Action Investment 2027</a></td><td headers="interest" data-title="Interest">2.1% p.a.</td><td headers="term" data-title="Term">5 years</td><td headers="amount" data-title="Amount raised">£339,000</td><td headers="close date" data-title="Close date">29 September 2022</td></tr></tbody></table></div></div></div></div></div></div></section><div class="bg-colour--primary-surface bg-mask bg-mask--b-convex ai-scope"></div><section class="home-financial m-y-spacer-md p-y-spacer-xl mx-auto choke-800 ai-scope"><div class="container"><div class="row"><div class="col-12"><div class="flex-center"><h2 class="text-center" data-content="1-143211">Creating a greener future for all their communities</h2></div><div class="flex-center"><p class="body--lg text-center choke-800 m-b-spacer-lg"><span data-content="2-143221"><span>In July 2019, the Council declared a&nbsp;<a href="https://www.sustainabletelfordandwrekin.com/what-the-council-is-doing/climate-emergency#" target="" rel="">climate emergency</a>&nbsp;and committed to ensure its activities and operations are&nbsp;<a href="https://www.sustainabletelfordandwrekin.com/what-the-council-is-doing/climate-emergency#" target="" rel="">carbon neutral</a>&nbsp;by 2030.&nbsp;<br></span><br><span>The Council resolved to work with partners to identify and implement adaptation and mitigation measures to deal with the effects of the ongoing changes in climate; and to collaborate and engage with local residents, partners and businesses to achieve their aspiration for the borough to be carbon neutral by 2030 – making sure they take communities with them, protect employment and without impoverishing their most deprived communities.</span></span></p></div><div class="flex flex-center"><figure class="brand-figure w-100"><img src="https://cdn4.sharein.com/abundance/cms/792a9dba-4824-4813-96d0-71166ff1c650.jpg" width="800" height="450" alt="Title placeholder text" loading="lazy"> <figcaption data-content="2-143224">Investors money has fund green projects across the borough.</figcaption></figure></div></div></div></div></section></div>
